---
description: Test first. See the failure. Then the smallest code.
alwaysApply: true
---

# TDD

- Name the behavior in one sentence.
- Add one failing test. Run that test and keep the failure.
- Write the smallest code that turns it green. Run it again.
- If production code was written before the failing test, delete that code and start from the test.
- One behavior per cycle.
- Close with `pytest -q` or `npm test` (`vitest run`). Do not use watch mode.
- Docs and prose do not need a test. Say so in the same turn. Production code does.
- Tests read a small fixture. They do not open WRDS.
